The address you followed does not name a page on this site. The link may be
stale, or the page may have moved.

The sidebar lists every page. The likeliest destinations:

- [Start building]($link.page('start')) is the first call, in every language.
- [Why OCapN]($link.page('why')) compares the ideas with the protocols you
  already use.
- [Concepts]($link.page('concepts')) explains the machinery one level down.
- [Choosing a transport]($link.page('transports/choosing')) compares the
  transports side by side.

If a link on this site brought you here, that is a defect worth reporting:
[open an issue](https://github.com/glowcap-org/glowcap/issues).

```=html
<script>
	// A deep link into the Rooms page lands here, because this host serves one
	// file per address. Hand the path to the page, which opens where it pointed.
	// The page's address is the one the header links, so it is written once.
	(function () {
		var link = document.querySelector("a[data-rooms-app]");
		if (link === null) return;
		var app = link.pathname;
		var path = location.pathname;
		if (path.indexOf(app) !== 0 || path === app) return;
		location.replace(app + "?path=" + encodeURIComponent(path.slice(app.length) + location.search) + location.hash);
	})();
</script>
```
